  "evidence": [
    "Fresh pinned and qualified production listings prove kill_landmark already uses DEC, so discarded-result decrement variants are not compiled. Its actual three-byte residual lies in inlined xrange: original reuses a loaded longitude register while current SUB reloads memory. base_coast shows the same shared family; the standalone helper remains exact.",
    "Retained actual helper-call versus hand-inlined and register-order trials do not show these three specific header forms previously measured. Keep the original low flat bit, no longitude read on the flat path, one adjustment only, int signedness/overflow behavior and all caller-visible operations. No volatile, flags, exports, class/layout or machine-code tricks.",
    "Pilot scope is private overlays of the two named source files and all mapped map.cpp identities, including header-owned helper bodies emitted there. Run an unchanged qualified-production object control and literal target damage; maximum three fixed compiler variants. Do not publish or claim project-wide improvement from this single-TU control.",
    "Before any shared-header publication, derive and admit affected caller/owner closure centrally, preserve all historical claims, independently review semantics, measure the full application and investigate regressions. No reset of the original baseline, automatic demotion, full linked/structure/runtime or game acceptance."
  ],
  "intent": "Pilot three ordinary guarded longitude-snapshot source forms in the genuine shared xrange helper, measuring the complete map owner TU before any source publication or wider migration.",
